title: The <span style="color: #000000;">**[+ unionist_party_name +]**</span> Disaffiliates with the the Banners
subtitle: Expectedly, the <span style="color: #000000;">Faithful</span> have left the <span style="color: #000000;">rep</span><span style="color: #DD0000;">ubl</span><span style="color: #FFCC00;">ican</span> organization.
view-if: not banner_exit and concord_formed
new-page: true
tags: event
on-display: {!  
    var cardEl = document.createElement('div');  
    cardEl.className = "face-figure2";  

    var image = new Image();  
    image.className = "face-img";  
    image.src = "img/reichsbanner_flag.jpg";  

    cardEl.appendChild(image);  
    var contentDiv = document.querySelector("#page #mid_panel #content");
    contentDiv.appendChild(cardEl);
!}
max-visits: 1

= The <span style="color: #000000;">**[+ unionist_party_name +]**</span> disaffiliates with the the Banners

The merger between the <span style="color: #000000;">Faithful</span> and the <span style="color: #3E88B3;">nationalists</span> has compelled them to disaffiliate from the the Banners, for obvious reasons. A small group from the <span style="color: #FF7F00;">Faithful Left</span> has remained in the organization, including figures like former Chancellor Joseph Werth, who has defied orders to resign from the party’s leadership. It is expected that he will leave the party in the near future.

In the meantime, the party is debating its stance on ties with the <span style="color: #3E88B3;">**Wardens**</span>, who are now awkwardly sandwiched between Mallin’s <span style="color: #003755;">**CNF**</span> and the <span style="color: #000000;">Faithful</span>.

- @let_go: Let the <span style="color: #000000;">Faithful</span> go.

@let_go
on-arrival: banner_strength *= 0.85; unionist_relation -= 5; lvp_relation -= 3; lvp_right += 3; pro_republic -= 5; concord_right += 3; concord_leave_banner = 1

Despite the vigorous protest from the <span style="color: #FF7F00;">Faithful Left</span> faction, and the refusal of ardent <span style="color: #000000;">repu</span><span style="color: #DD0000;">bli</span><span style="color: #FFCC00;">cans</span> like Werth to leave, this has dealt a significant blow to the organization. With the <span style="color: #000000;">Faithful</span> gone, the the Banners, in the public's eye, is nothing more than a <span style="color: #c00000;">Reformist</span> militia.

The <span style="color: #3E88B3;">**Wardens**</span> has reaffirmed political neutrality, but leans closer to the more politically successful <span style="color: #000000;">**[+ unionist_party_name +]**</span>.

- @wirth_spd
- @wirth_retire

@wirth_spd
title: Joseph Werth has used this as a pretext to announce his resignation from the <span style="color: #000000;">**[+ unionist_party_name +]**</span>.
view-if: reformist_strength >= center_strength + left_strength
on-arrival: commons_unionist -= 2; commons_marcher += 4; faithful_unionist -= 2; faithful_marcher += 4; wirth_marcher = 1
face-image: img/portraits/wirth.jpg

Werth, who has always been a close friend of the <span style="color: #c00000;">**Marchers**</span>—and who likely would have joined us long ago were it not for our <span style="color: #9B0000;">Vaelist</span> foundations—has officially defected to the <span style="color: #c00000;">**Marchers**</span>! He’s done this before as a temporary protest against his party’s right wing, but this time, it looks like he’s here to stay. Our reformist party platform played a major role in overcoming his earlier hesitation.

Unfortunately, this seems to be a lone defection. The <span style="color: #FF7F00;">Faithful Left</span> faction has largely remained within the <span style="color: #000000;">**[+ unionist_party_name +]**</span>, where they hold little real power and operate more as a pressure group than an influential bloc. [? if neorevisionism: Joseph Werth has joined the Neorevisionist faction, owing to his impassioned support of the Unity Republic. ?]

@wirth_retire
title: Joseph Werth has used this as a pretext to announce his resignation from the <span style="color: #000000;">**[+ unionist_party_name +]**</span>.
view-if: reformist_strength < center_strength + left_strength
on-arrival: commons_unionist -= 2; faithful_unionist -= 2
face-image: img/portraits/wirth.jpg

Werth, long a thorn in the side of the former <span style="color: #000000;">Unionists</span> due to his leftist leanings, has now left its more right-wing successor. He had considered joining the <span style="color: #c00000;">**Marchers**</span>, but our <span style="color: #9B0000;">Vaelist</span> course ultimately alienated him from that path. He has since retired from party politics and now focuses on chairing various <span style="color: #000000;">rep</span><span style="color: #DD0000;">ubl</span><span style="color: #FFCC00;">ican</span> and Faithful organizations.

Unfortunately, this remains a lone defection. The <span style="color: #FF7F00;">Faithful Left</span> faction has largely stayed within the <span style="color: #000000;">[+ unionist_party_name +]</span>, where they wield little actual power and function more as a pressure group than a meaningful political force.